language Essence 1.3

$ A partial function need not define every value in its domain, so f(y) is undefined wherever f
$ defines nothing and the constraint it sits in is false there: y has to be the one value f does
$ define.
find f : function (size 1) int(1..2) --> int(1)
find y : int(1..2)
such that f(y) = 1
